---
description: "Pericles Plans core standards for incident response planning, workflows, communications, and decision support integrated with Atlas, Events, and Insights"
globs: "*"
alwaysApply: false
---

<rule>
  <meta>
    <title>Pericles Plans Core Standards</title>
    <description>Defines core standards for creating, executing, and improving incident response plans with deep integration to Atlas, Events, and Insights.</description>
  </meta>
  <requirements>
    <requirement priority="high">
      <description>Define business goals and objectives for Plans aligned to organizational resilience and MTTR reduction.</description>
      <examples>
        <example title="Business Goals">
          <correct-example><![CDATA[
Goals documented and visible within Plans admin UI.
Objectives traceable to measurable KPIs (e.g., MTTR, response coverage).
]]></correct-example>
        </example>
      </examples>
    </requirement>
    <requirement priority="high">
      <description>Capture user stories for all primary roles (CISO, IT, Comms, HR, Operations) across plan lifecycle.</description>
      <examples>
        <example title="User Stories">
          <correct-example><![CDATA[
Backlog of role-based user stories exists with acceptance criteria.
Stories trace to features and tests in CI.
]]></correct-example>
        </example>
      </examples>
    </requirement>
    <requirement priority="critical">
      <description>Implement role-based access, tenant isolation, and audit logging for all plan actions.</description>
      <examples>
        <example title="Security & Audit">
          <correct-example><![CDATA[
Unauthorized actions return 403 and are logged.
All create/update/delete/export actions generate audit entries with user, time, scope.
]]></correct-example>
        </example>
      </examples>
    </requirement>
    <requirement priority="high">
      <description>Ensure performance targets for UI interactions and exports under realistic loads.</description>
      <examples>
        <example title="Performance Targets">
          <correct-example><![CDATA[
Dashboard P95 load < 2s on warm cache; interactions 60 FPS; exports complete under 30s P95.
Tables are virtualized; queries paginated and indexed.
]]></correct-example>
        </example>
      </examples>
    </requirement>
    <requirement priority="high">
      <description>Accessibility conformance at WCAG 2.1 AA for all user-facing components.</description>
      <examples>
        <example title="Accessibility">
          <correct-example><![CDATA[
Automated a11y scans show zero critical violations.
Keyboard navigation and ARIA labeling validated on core flows.
]]></correct-example>
        </example>
      </examples>
    </requirement>
  </requirements>
  <context description="Plans Features, Integrations, Compliance, and Notes">
    <![CDATA[
Features:
  core:
    - title: Plan Creation & Customization
      description: Templates for common scenarios with organizational customization and version control.
      options: ["cyber breach", "ransomware", "natural disaster", "supply chain disruption", "workplace violence"]
    - title: Roles, Responsibilities & Escalation Paths
      description: Role-based assignments and escalation workflows with directory integration.
      options: ["CISO", "IT", "Communications", "HR", "Legal", "Operations"]
    - title: Automated Response Workflows
      description: Task orchestration with completion tracking, conditional branching, and tool integrations.
      options: ["Conditional playbooks", "Jira", "ServiceNow", "SIEM", "SOAR"]
    - title: Communication & Collaboration
      description: Centralized communications, multi-channel alerts, Slack/Teams integration, and PR templates.
      options: ["email", "SMS", "push notifications", "voice calls", "Slack", "Microsoft Teams"]
    - title: Monitoring & Detection Integrations
      description: Ingest feeds from SIEM/EDR/threat intel and auto-generate incidents upon triggers.
      options: ["SIEM", "EDR", "Threat Intelligence"]
    - title: Simulation & Testing (Tabletop Exercises)
      description: Built-in drills, scenario tracking, outcomes analysis, and improvement recommendations.
      options: ["tabletop scenarios", "automated recommendations"]
    - title: Audit, Reporting & Compliance
      description: Detailed logs, communications, action histories, and regulatory reporting with dashboards.
      options: ["ISO 27001", "NIST", "HIPAA", "GDPR", "MTTR metrics"]
    - title: Post-Incident Review & Continuous Improvement
      description: Root cause analysis, linkage to risk registers/mitigation plans, and lessons learned.
      options: ["RCA", "risk register linkage", "playbook updates"]
  premium:
    - title: AI-driven Recommendations
      description: Prioritize responses and resources using AI based on incident context.
      options: ["priority suggestions", "confidence scoring"]
    - title: Geospatial Risk Mapping
      description: Physical incident overlays and proximity analysis in Atlas for plan activation.
      options: ["facility proximity", "route impact"]
    - title: Third-Party Coordination
      description: Workflows for vendors, regulators, insurers with secure collaboration.
      options: ["external invites", "document exchange"]
    - title: Mobile-first Field Operations
      description: Optimized mobile access for on-site actions and updates.
      options: ["offline-ready", "push actions"]

Integrations: ["Jira", "ServiceNow", "Slack", "Microsoft Teams", "SIEM", "SOAR", "EDR", "Threat Intelligence", "Email/SMS/Push/Voice Providers", "HR/IT Directory"]
Compliance: ["ISO 27001", "NIST", "HIPAA", "GDPR"]
Auditing:
  enabled: true
  notes: All plan lifecycle actions (create/update/activate/escalate/close/export) are audited with user, timestamp, scope, and diff.
Notes: UI color palette and detailed styling follow Admin Portal/Atlas standards; specific provider details for HR/IT directories and voice providers may vary by tenant and are noted as integrations.
    ]]>
  </context>
</rule>